# Doer — AI Goal-Scheduling Calendar App

**Spec version:** 1.0 · **Date:** 2026-09-26 · **Status:** Approved architecture, pre-implementation

A mobile app for ambitious people with big goals. Users describe their goals, attach context documents, and import their existing calendars. An LLM decomposes goals into atomic, duration-bounded tasks and assigns each to a day. A deterministic on-device engine places tasks into free time, writes them to a dedicated device calendar, and re-plans on request when the user falls behind.

---

## 1. Architecture Overview

**Zero backend.** The Flutter client calls the LLM provider directly over HTTPS. No GPU host, no proxy, no API server, no database server. All state lives in on-device SQLite; all arithmetic is deterministic Dart.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph Client["Flutter client (Android)"]
        UI["Agenda UI"] <--> DB[("SQLite\nsource of truth")]
        Slotter["Dart slotter"] <--> DB
        Slotter --> Cal["device_calendar\n"My Plan" calendar"]
        UI --> Slotter
        Extract["Text extraction\n(TXT/PDF/DOCX)"] --> LLM["Provider adapter\n+ JSON schema validation"]
        ICSIn[".ics import\n(busy blocks)"] --> DB
        Slotter --> LLM
    end
    LLM -->|"HTTPS + response_format"| P{"Provider"}
    P -->|"demo key\n(capped, cheap model)"| Hosted["Hosted provider"]
    P -->|"user key"| Byok["OpenAI / Anthropic / Gemini /\nOpenRouter / custom base URL\n(self-hosted vLLM)"]
```

### 1.1 Invariants

1. **LLM does semantics only.** It decomposes goals into tasks and judges *which day* a task belongs on. It never computes times, durations-of-fit, feasibility, or interval math. `scheduled_start`/`scheduled_end` are slotter-owned.
2. **Completion is monotonic.** A `completed` task is frozen forever; re-planning touches only unfinished work.
3. **SQLite is the source of truth.** The device calendar is a projection; every written event id (`device_event_id`) maps back to a task row.
4. **The app writes exactly one calendar** — `"My Plan"` — and never reads beyond busy-block ingestion or writes anything outside it.
5. **All provider output is schema-validated** with at most one automatic repair retry, then fail-fast.
6. **Local-first.** Everything except decomposition and full re-plan works offline.
7. **Priorities are explicit user decisions** (P1–P3), never AI triage.

