## 12. Verification & Acceptance Criteria

**Unit (slotter):** free-segment math with fixture busy blocks (work windows, buffers, overlap, RRULE expansions, TZID/UTC); priority ordering; dependency day-push; spill-forward + compression + adjust flagging; pinned-deadline clamping.

**Unit (providers):** adapter contract against a mock server; schema-repair retry fires exactly once; error mapping (401/402/429/5xx); demo-mode banner on quota errors.

**Unit (.ics parser):** fixture files covering recurring events, zoned and UTC times, all-day events.

**Integration (device/emulator):** `"My Plan"` creation; event write; atomic re-plan rewrite deletes unfinished events and preserves completed ones; skip re-slot moves exactly the affected events.

**End-to-end acceptance:**
1. Fresh install → agenda opens on demo key, no gate.
2. Create P1 goal with target date + PDF → decompose → tasks slotted across days within working hours, busy-imported time respected.
3. Import personal `.ics` → next decompose/re-plan avoids busy blocks.
4. Mark task Done → frozen forever; calendar event remains.
5. Tap Didn't Start on another → instantly re-slotted locally (offline), device calendar event moves, "adjusted" marker shown.
6. Request re-plan → LLM re-dates unfinished tasks; `"My Plan"` atomically rewritten; completed events untouched; tips displayed.
7. Simulate demo-key 402 → banner appears, deep-links to settings; all local features keep working.

